Follow-up to k283. Since k283, OCP::Kubernetes->_build_api calls OCP::K8s->register itself, and register is lazy (it pushes onto `$api->with`, and does nothing if the entry is already there). Three callers still call register on an api that OCP::Kubernetes already registered:
- robocop: OCP::Robocop::Controller::_build_kube (robocop lane). Its comment "without which OCPNode and OCPNodeProvider are not addressable" no longer holds.
- OCP::Cmd::SSH::_node_names and _lookup_by_name (apply/ssh lane).

These calls are harmless but misleading. Done = remove them, fix the comment, and keep t/229, t/235, t/237 and the robocop controller tests green. If a caller builds its api without OCP::Kubernetes, keep its call.

